WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:03.271
(zooming)

00:00:03.271 --> 00:00:04.104
- What's up Believe Nation?

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:06.122
It's Evan, my one word is believe

00:00:06.122 --> 00:00:09.494
and I believe in people more
than they believe in themselves

00:00:09.494 --> 00:00:12.656
and my sincere hope is
that if you see in yourself

00:00:12.656 --> 00:00:16.653
what I see in you, you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:16.653 --> 00:00:17.897
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:17.897 --> 00:00:19.480
I started the Did You Know series

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.937
to try to get to know some of
the successful entrepreneurs

00:00:21.937 --> 00:00:24.367
we've profiled in a little
bit more personal way.

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:26.507
Share some surprising facts about them

00:00:26.507 --> 00:00:28.038
that maybe you don't know yet

00:00:28.038 --> 00:00:30.457
and give you a little bit of a inside peek

00:00:30.457 --> 00:00:32.271
into their lives and who they are.

00:00:32.271 --> 00:00:35.319
So today we're going to
learn nine surprising facts

00:00:35.319 --> 00:00:37.110
about Oprah Winfrey.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.610
(theme music)

00:00:47.835 --> 00:00:48.740
(bell rings)

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.810
Fact number one, her
original name was Orpah

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:54.454
after the biblical character
in the Book of Ruth

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:55.849
and her aunt named her that.

00:00:55.849 --> 00:00:57.396
It's on her birth certificate,

00:00:57.396 --> 00:01:00.210
but so many people mispronounced
it and called her Oprah

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.562
that eventually the name just stuck.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:06.729
- I was born, as I said, in
rural Mississippi in 1954

00:01:07.594 --> 00:01:09.881
and I was born at home

00:01:09.881 --> 00:01:14.048
and there were not a lot
of educated people around

00:01:15.851 --> 00:01:19.512
and my name had been
chosen from the Bible.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.150
My Aunt Ida had chosen the name,

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:23.068
but nobody really knew how to spell it

00:01:23.068 --> 00:01:27.068
so it went down as Orpah
on my birth certificate

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:30.958
but people didn't know
how to pronounce it.

00:01:30.958 --> 00:01:35.881
So they put the P before
the R in every place else

00:01:35.881 --> 00:01:37.095
other than the birth certificate.

00:01:37.095 --> 00:01:39.073
So on the birth certificate it is Orpah

00:01:39.073 --> 00:01:42.520
but then it got translated
to Oprah and so here we are

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.343
but that's great because
Oprah spells Harpo backwards.

00:01:46.343 --> 00:01:49.294
I don't know what Orpah spells.

00:01:49.294 --> 00:01:50.193
(bell rings)

00:01:50.193 --> 00:01:54.404
- Fact number two, 50 Cent
named his dog Oprah after her

00:01:54.404 --> 00:01:57.525
and his cat after her best friend, Gail.

00:01:57.525 --> 00:02:01.389
- Let me ask you, I heard
you have a dog named Oprah?

00:02:01.389 --> 00:02:02.222
- Yes.

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.277
- I consider that a compliment,

00:02:03.277 --> 00:02:05.003
whether you meant it to be one or not.

00:02:05.003 --> 00:02:06.303
- Yeah, I love her, I love you.

00:02:06.303 --> 00:02:07.611
(Oprah laughs)

00:02:07.611 --> 00:02:10.122
You know when then say a
dog's a man's best friend?

00:02:10.122 --> 00:02:13.460
- Yeah, I know, I've
had 22 dogs in my life.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:14.559
I have five right now.

00:02:14.559 --> 00:02:16.070
Okay, but you named your dog Oprah,

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:17.474
that was not the compliment.

00:02:17.474 --> 00:02:19.563
- I added a cat, I got a cat too.

00:02:19.563 --> 00:02:20.640
- [Oprah] Name?
- Gail.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.918
(Oprah laughs)

00:02:21.918 --> 00:02:22.751
You know I was just lookin'

00:02:22.751 --> 00:02:25.475
for a real cute names for the pets

00:02:25.475 --> 00:02:26.308
that people would--

00:02:26.308 --> 00:02:27.323
- Do you still have the dog named Oprah?

00:02:27.323 --> 00:02:29.573
- Yeah, I got a babysitter
for her when I travel.

00:02:29.573 --> 00:02:31.206
- Wow, you have a dog nanny.

00:02:31.206 --> 00:02:32.125
I call it dog nanny.

00:02:32.125 --> 00:02:33.797
- Dog nanny.
- Dog nanny.

00:02:33.797 --> 00:02:35.877
- Okay, why'd you name your dog Oprah?

00:02:35.877 --> 00:02:38.152
- At the time I was just
looking at the situation

00:02:38.152 --> 00:02:41.536
and saw I was developin' negative feelings

00:02:41.536 --> 00:02:43.039
for someone who doesn't even know me.

00:02:43.039 --> 00:02:44.454
- Yeah.

00:02:44.454 --> 00:02:46.053
- And then I gave it to the dog

00:02:46.053 --> 00:02:48.339
cause I was excited about
the dog at the time.

00:02:48.339 --> 00:02:50.697
- So now do you have
greater affection for me.

00:02:50.697 --> 00:02:53.495
- Absolutely, I have for
you for a few years now.

00:02:53.495 --> 00:02:56.698
I take pictures and say
crazy stuff on Twitter

00:02:56.698 --> 00:02:59.925
but people impact because
they would associate it to me

00:02:59.925 --> 00:03:00.758
saying it to you.

00:03:00.758 --> 00:03:02.074
- I know.

00:03:02.074 --> 00:03:03.042
(bell rings)

00:03:03.042 --> 00:03:04.988
- Fact number three, she helped

00:03:04.988 --> 00:03:07.900
to launch Doctor Phil's career.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.557
- I feel like I raised this dude.

00:03:09.557 --> 00:03:11.016
And let me just tell ya,

00:03:11.016 --> 00:03:15.183
I had a moment driving in
and seeing your big face

00:03:17.172 --> 00:03:20.167
on the side of the Paramount wall.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:22.102
I must say wow!

00:03:22.102 --> 00:03:23.786
(audience applause)

00:03:23.786 --> 00:03:24.619
Wow, wow!

00:03:26.546 --> 00:03:28.004
(audience applause)

00:03:28.004 --> 00:03:30.241
And it all started cause we going through,

00:03:30.241 --> 00:03:32.320
I was going through a hard time.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:33.418
- What was it, 98?

00:03:33.418 --> 00:03:34.505
- It was 98.

00:03:34.505 --> 00:03:36.475
- And we worked for two years before that.

00:03:36.475 --> 00:03:37.308
- [Oprah] That's right.

00:03:37.308 --> 00:03:39.403
- So we been knowin' each other 20 years.

00:03:39.403 --> 00:03:43.347
- No, I was knowing,
Jay was in high school.

00:03:43.347 --> 00:03:45.962
- Cause I remember Jay,
came time for you to testify

00:03:45.962 --> 00:03:47.378
and you said not unless Jay's here.

00:03:47.378 --> 00:03:48.539
- Jay's here, yeah.

00:03:48.539 --> 00:03:50.308
- She called Jay's high school

00:03:50.308 --> 00:03:52.900
and said I need him out of class

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:56.177
and the principal went
to his class and said

00:03:56.177 --> 00:03:58.901
"Somebody that sounded a
whole lot like Oprah Winfrey."

00:03:58.901 --> 00:03:59.734
- Like Oprah Winfrey.

00:03:59.734 --> 00:04:00.620
(audience laughs)

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:03.131
- "Just called and said
they need Jay out of class."

00:04:03.131 --> 00:04:03.964
- You know what it was,

00:04:03.964 --> 00:04:05.218
cause Jay and I became friends

00:04:05.218 --> 00:04:07.147
and I just wanted
somebody to hold my hand.

00:04:07.147 --> 00:04:10.103
So we did that trial
and then I said to Phil,

00:04:10.103 --> 00:04:11.860
I wanted you to come on television

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:16.027
and do for the other people
what you had done for me.

00:04:17.262 --> 00:04:18.306
(bell rings)

00:04:18.306 --> 00:04:22.281
- Fact number four, she once
competed in Miss Black America.

00:04:22.281 --> 00:04:26.665
- I remember back in 19 blah
blah, when I was a contestant,

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:29.951
that I just was so
excited about being there.

00:04:29.951 --> 00:04:34.197
I considered it a major
accomplishment just to get there

00:04:34.197 --> 00:04:36.338
and represent my state, Tennessee.

00:04:36.338 --> 00:04:38.714
And I remember being so nervous and upset

00:04:38.714 --> 00:04:40.667
when all the girls,

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:41.934
at least I thought all the girls,

00:04:41.934 --> 00:04:43.613
at least appeared to be all the girls,

00:04:43.613 --> 00:04:46.557
got flowers from home
from their boyfriends

00:04:46.557 --> 00:04:48.535
and I was dating this dud at the time

00:04:48.535 --> 00:04:52.513
who did not send me not even
one single solitary rose

00:04:52.513 --> 00:04:54.421
and I remember being so upset about it

00:04:54.421 --> 00:04:56.815
and it was Miss Iowa who said to me

00:04:56.815 --> 00:05:00.083
"It really doesn't matter if
you put a flower on your mind."

00:05:00.083 --> 00:05:02.827
And so I let that kind of
carry me through the contest

00:05:02.827 --> 00:05:04.804
having that flower in my mind

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.938
and believing anything was possible

00:05:06.938 --> 00:05:09.340
and just enjoying the experience.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:11.186
And although I didn't place,

00:05:11.186 --> 00:05:15.101
I went home with a flower in
my mind feelin' pretty good.

00:05:15.101 --> 00:05:15.934
(bell rings)

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:17.954
- Fact number five is
she considered starting

00:05:17.954 --> 00:05:19.563
a girls school in Africa

00:05:19.563 --> 00:05:22.616
to be one of her greatest accomplishments.

00:05:22.616 --> 00:05:25.533
- As a mother, as just a person who

00:05:27.034 --> 00:05:30.972
has been a part of your lives
for the past four, five years,

00:05:30.972 --> 00:05:32.402
I've never been more proud.

00:05:32.402 --> 00:05:35.705
I think you all were exemplary.

00:05:35.705 --> 00:05:37.865
You made me a really proud Momma.

00:05:37.865 --> 00:05:39.954
- [Juju] She may not
have biological children,

00:05:39.954 --> 00:05:41.609
but thanks to the first graduates

00:05:41.609 --> 00:05:44.610
of the Oprah Winfrey
Leadership Academy for Girls,

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:48.355
Oprah says she now understands
the trials and tribulations,

00:05:48.355 --> 00:05:50.648
as well as the joys, of parenthood.

00:05:50.648 --> 00:05:52.069
- Nice to see you!

00:05:52.069 --> 00:05:53.796
- All seen in the documentary

00:05:53.796 --> 00:05:56.021
The First Graduating Class.

00:05:56.021 --> 00:05:58.402
So when they call you Mom
Oprah, that's for real.

00:05:58.402 --> 00:06:00.642
- Juju, if you were there
more than 10 minutes,

00:06:00.642 --> 00:06:03.181
they'd call you Sis Juju.

00:06:03.181 --> 00:06:05.383
- No matter who you're with,
no matter what you're doing,

00:06:05.383 --> 00:06:08.022
if one of these girls calls,
you pick up the phone.

00:06:08.022 --> 00:06:09.863
- Oh yes, now we're all
texting all the time.

00:06:09.863 --> 00:06:11.835
As a matter of fact that
just happened this morning

00:06:11.835 --> 00:06:13.912
and I was on the phone
last night for an hour

00:06:13.912 --> 00:06:16.001
with one of 'em trying
to watch the debate.

00:06:16.001 --> 00:06:16.907
(Juju laughs)

00:06:16.907 --> 00:06:18.241
I was like okay, trying
to watch the debate

00:06:18.241 --> 00:06:21.016
but okay I hear what you're saying.

00:06:21.016 --> 00:06:24.598
Yes, I think I've come
into my mothering space

00:06:24.598 --> 00:06:28.515
in a way that was wholly,
wholly so unexpected.

00:06:31.864 --> 00:06:34.373
I knew from the moment
that I met these girls

00:06:34.373 --> 00:06:37.068
that I was going to fall in
love with them and I did.

00:06:37.068 --> 00:06:39.624
- [Juju] The maternal
bonding began five years ago

00:06:39.624 --> 00:06:42.059
as a leap of philanthropic faith,

00:06:42.059 --> 00:06:44.705
inspired by the venerable Nelson Mandela.

00:06:44.705 --> 00:06:47.622
- What is the single life changing,

00:06:49.871 --> 00:06:52.621
trajectory changing moment for me

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:57.257
was being exposed to a world of education

00:06:57.257 --> 00:07:00.953
that offered me a new insight
into how I saw the world.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:04.871
So I just wanted to do that
for somebody else, that's all.

00:07:04.871 --> 00:07:05.704
(bell rings)

00:07:05.704 --> 00:07:07.562
- Fact number six, she
started going to school

00:07:07.562 --> 00:07:09.858
at the age of six,
already knew how to read

00:07:09.858 --> 00:07:12.647
and was consistently
ahead of her classmates.

00:07:12.647 --> 00:07:16.548
- First day I went to
school, I was in a classroom,

00:07:16.548 --> 00:07:19.215
by the time I was six years old,

00:07:20.105 --> 00:07:21.219
didn't go to school
till I was six years old

00:07:21.219 --> 00:07:23.024
cause I was living with my
Grandmother at that time.

00:07:23.024 --> 00:07:24.895
But she had taught me how
to read, read the Bible,

00:07:24.895 --> 00:07:26.056
Bible stories.

00:07:26.056 --> 00:07:30.420
So I went into the
classroom knowing Nicodemus,

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.798
Shadrach Meshach and Abednego,

00:07:32.798 --> 00:07:34.953
I could spell all of those words.

00:07:34.953 --> 00:07:39.032
I thought I was preachin'
to my kindergarten teacher.

00:07:39.032 --> 00:07:42.496
So she was like who is this girl?

00:07:42.496 --> 00:07:45.968
So I was never placed in an environment

00:07:45.968 --> 00:07:49.253
where I was ever made to feel inferior.

00:07:49.253 --> 00:07:52.610
I always felt like I'm the
smartest kid in this room.

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:55.576
And because I was never placed,

00:07:55.576 --> 00:07:59.405
never put in a position where
I was made to feel less than,

00:07:59.405 --> 00:08:02.086
I didn't grow up feeling
less than, you know?

00:08:02.086 --> 00:08:03.751
- And the rest as they say is history.

00:08:03.751 --> 00:08:05.183
- And the rest they say is history.

00:08:05.183 --> 00:08:06.706
And it's all about what you believe.

00:08:06.706 --> 00:08:09.187
You know I say this too,

00:08:09.187 --> 00:08:12.724
when I do something on my
network now called Life Class.

00:08:12.724 --> 00:08:16.891
The fundamental key to
success is what you believe

00:08:18.593 --> 00:08:19.869
is true for yourself.

00:08:19.869 --> 00:08:22.759
Not what you want, not what you desire.

00:08:22.759 --> 00:08:24.225
It's what do you believe.

00:08:24.225 --> 00:08:26.783
You can say I want to be
the most successful person

00:08:26.783 --> 00:08:27.616
in the world,

00:08:27.616 --> 00:08:29.362
but if you believe that
there's a glass ceiling

00:08:29.362 --> 00:08:30.810
and you're going to have a hard time

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.602
kicking through that glass ceiling,

00:08:32.602 --> 00:08:35.015
you will be defined by the glass ceiling.

00:08:35.015 --> 00:08:38.116
And the great beauty and gift of my life

00:08:38.116 --> 00:08:41.321
is that I was never defined by the box

00:08:41.321 --> 00:08:43.407
that other people tried to put me in.

00:08:43.407 --> 00:08:44.240
(bell rings)

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:47.308
- Fact number seven, in 2011 she received

00:08:47.308 --> 00:08:51.349
an honorary Oscar for her
philanthropic efforts.

00:08:51.349 --> 00:08:55.841
- It's unimaginable that I
would be standing before you

00:08:55.841 --> 00:08:58.508
voted by the Board of Governors.

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:03.378
(audience applause)

00:09:03.378 --> 00:09:06.240
- [Announcer] Drama at the
Governors Awards as Oprah Winfrey

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:09.263
accepted the Jean Hersholt's
Humanitarian Award

00:09:09.263 --> 00:09:12.639
from the Academy of Motion
Picture Arts and Sciences.

00:09:12.639 --> 00:09:14.868
- I don't know of anyone, anyone,

00:09:14.868 --> 00:09:17.246
who would be more deserving.

00:09:17.246 --> 00:09:20.334
- What this really means
is that all of us can make

00:09:20.334 --> 00:09:23.278
a difference through
the life that we live.

00:09:23.278 --> 00:09:26.075
- [Announcer] Oprah, Oscar
nominated for The Color Purple,

00:09:26.075 --> 00:09:28.198
was honored for her philanthropy.

00:09:28.198 --> 00:09:31.483
- She's always thinking about
how she can help others.

00:09:31.483 --> 00:09:34.417
- Increasing the literacy
level of this country

00:09:34.417 --> 00:09:36.651
by your mere passion for books.

00:09:36.651 --> 00:09:37.484
(bell rings)

00:09:37.484 --> 00:09:40.661
- Fact number eight, she ran
the Marine Corp. Marathon

00:09:40.661 --> 00:09:43.015
with her trainer, Bob Green.

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:44.833
- I vowed that I was
going to run a marathon

00:09:44.833 --> 00:09:47.213
even though I was all
blowed up at the time.

00:09:47.213 --> 00:09:48.046
Agreed?

00:09:48.046 --> 00:09:49.455
(audience laughs)

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:51.104
That I was going to work on myself

00:09:51.104 --> 00:09:55.098
and I was going to run a
marathon by the time I turned 40.

00:09:55.098 --> 00:09:56.522
Well it was my biggest dream ever

00:09:56.522 --> 00:09:59.544
and for months, for months
you know you have to train

00:09:59.544 --> 00:10:02.334
so that you can handle the 26 miles.

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:04.825
Here's some of the training.

00:10:04.825 --> 00:10:07.507
Okay, so this is August 9th

00:10:07.507 --> 00:10:11.674
and we're about eight and a
half miles into a 15 mile run.

00:10:13.024 --> 00:10:17.191
All a part of the training
for the 26 mile marathon.

00:10:18.429 --> 00:10:22.596
I've been running now for
exactly two hours straight.

00:10:24.251 --> 00:10:25.084
Exactly.

00:10:27.282 --> 00:10:31.032
I had to stop to wee
willy winkle four times.

00:10:32.685 --> 00:10:34.941
It's a bad willy winkle day for me.

00:10:34.941 --> 00:10:37.497
(barking)

00:10:37.497 --> 00:10:41.330
Bob just said "Hey, got
some good news for ya.

00:10:43.255 --> 00:10:46.557
"After today you only
have 10 more long runs

00:10:46.557 --> 00:10:49.320
"like this one till the marathon."

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:51.570
(laughing)

00:10:52.578 --> 00:10:54.144
He calls that good news!

00:10:54.144 --> 00:10:56.394
(laughing)

00:10:58.328 --> 00:11:01.359
I'm ready to die and you
think that's good news!

00:11:01.359 --> 00:11:03.609
(laughing)

00:11:04.914 --> 00:11:07.497
Don't tell me no bad news okay.

00:11:08.794 --> 00:11:11.355
Okay, so that was just
a part of the training.

00:11:11.355 --> 00:11:13.803
Two weeks ago I ran the
Marine Corps Marathon

00:11:13.803 --> 00:11:16.243
in Washington D.C. and
this was the real deal.

00:11:16.243 --> 00:11:20.681
We got to the race site about
an hour before the start time.

00:11:20.681 --> 00:11:22.281
It was pouring rain.

00:11:22.281 --> 00:11:24.031
Hadn't expected that.

00:11:25.431 --> 00:11:27.164
As I made my way to the start

00:11:27.164 --> 00:11:30.584
I was feeling a little
nervous really, anxious

00:11:30.584 --> 00:11:32.690
and a lot of pressure

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:35.118
as all the photographers surrounded us.

00:11:35.118 --> 00:11:37.077
- [Man] Alright guys, give me a path here.

00:11:37.077 --> 00:11:37.910
Move it!

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:40.280
- [Oprah] I was thinking what
have I gotten myself into?

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:42.287
I finally made it through the crowds.

00:11:42.287 --> 00:11:46.454
Their spirit hadn't been
dampened at all by the downpour.

00:11:47.341 --> 00:11:48.724
- [Woman] Good luck Oprah!

00:11:48.724 --> 00:11:49.974
- Yeah! Thanks!

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:55.713
And then I got my last
little good luck hug in

00:11:55.713 --> 00:11:59.880
and tried to calm myself as
the national anthem played.

00:12:03.459 --> 00:12:05.709
(applause)

00:12:08.325 --> 00:12:10.493
I was really anxious to get going.

00:12:10.493 --> 00:12:14.660
The starting gun sounded,
15,000 runners took off at once.

00:12:19.356 --> 00:12:22.048
I knew they were going to
swallow me and they did.

00:12:22.048 --> 00:12:23.553
I was swallowed by the massive pack

00:12:23.553 --> 00:12:25.636
of all those marathoners.

00:12:30.837 --> 00:12:33.081
About 37 minutes into the run,

00:12:33.081 --> 00:12:35.357
I looked at my watch
and said remember this

00:12:35.357 --> 00:12:38.107
cause you're feeling pretty good.

00:12:39.748 --> 00:12:43.284
Two tabloid reporters were so
dead set on getting the scoop

00:12:43.284 --> 00:12:47.317
on my first marathon they
actually ran the race

00:12:47.317 --> 00:12:49.201
alongside me.

00:12:49.201 --> 00:12:53.373
This is David from the National Enquirer.

00:12:53.373 --> 00:12:55.130
Peter ran the whole way for 13 miles.

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:55.963
- I'm still here!

00:12:55.963 --> 00:12:57.758
- David came to meet us back there.

00:12:57.758 --> 00:12:59.193
This was my worst nightmare.

00:12:59.193 --> 00:13:01.830
I had to pee and there's
the National Enquirer

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:03.413
running next to me.

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:09.784
At mile 16 I'd been running
for almost three hours.

00:13:09.784 --> 00:13:13.951
We rounded the Capital, I
was feeling pretty good.

00:13:17.353 --> 00:13:20.889
As you can see the rain wasn't letting up.

00:13:20.889 --> 00:13:24.556
Miles 19 through 21,
whoa, those were tough!

00:13:25.442 --> 00:13:27.375
Lots of runners were dropping out,

00:13:27.375 --> 00:13:31.164
slowing down, walking,
just too tired go on.

00:13:31.164 --> 00:13:32.299
I'd been running at that point

00:13:32.299 --> 00:13:35.854
for about over four hours
and I was starting to hurt.

00:13:35.854 --> 00:13:37.521
The crowd was great.

00:13:38.581 --> 00:13:40.713
As I was nearing the final few miles,

00:13:40.713 --> 00:13:42.718
the momentum of the
crowd helped to carry me

00:13:42.718 --> 00:13:43.647
to the finish line.

00:13:43.647 --> 00:13:46.311
(crowd cheering)

00:13:46.311 --> 00:13:48.586
People always said it
would feel like this.

00:13:48.586 --> 00:13:52.753
And it was the greatest feeling
I believe I've ever had.

00:13:55.066 --> 00:13:57.803
I started to cry when I
saw that 26 mile marker

00:13:57.803 --> 00:14:01.354
and realized my dream
had really come true.

00:14:01.354 --> 00:14:02.187
I did it!

00:14:04.082 --> 00:14:05.702
I did it.

00:14:05.702 --> 00:14:08.285
I actually run a full marathon.

00:14:11.801 --> 00:14:12.888
(bell rings)

00:14:12.888 --> 00:14:15.266
- And fact number nine,
for a period of time

00:14:15.266 --> 00:14:18.683
she sang the theme song for her own show.

00:14:24.649 --> 00:14:27.982
♫ Ohhhh, run on, run on

00:14:31.382 --> 00:14:33.528
♫ Run on, run on

00:14:33.528 --> 00:14:36.121
♫ I believe I run on

00:14:36.121 --> 00:14:38.332
♫ See what the end will be

00:14:38.332 --> 00:14:40.150
♫ Believe I work on

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:42.391
♫ Find out what waits for me

00:14:42.391 --> 00:14:46.592
♫ I see 10,000 stories
and glories and dreams

00:14:46.592 --> 00:14:50.399
♫ See angles right here on Earth

00:14:50.399 --> 00:14:53.423
♫ I see laughing and growing and loving

00:14:53.423 --> 00:14:57.119
♫ And knowing what life is worth

00:14:57.119 --> 00:15:00.728
♫ So I believe I run on

00:15:00.728 --> 00:15:03.266
♫ And see what tomorrow will be

00:15:03.266 --> 00:15:05.239
♫ Run on, run on

00:15:05.239 --> 00:15:07.264
♫ Cause I like what I see

00:15:07.264 --> 00:15:09.078
♫ Run on, run on

00:15:09.078 --> 00:15:11.256
♫ Come on and run with me

00:15:11.256 --> 00:15:13.619
♫ Run on, run on

00:15:13.619 --> 00:15:14.997
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:15:14.997 --> 00:15:16.935
I'd love to know what did
you think of this video?

00:15:16.935 --> 00:15:18.754
Did you learn something new about Oprah

00:15:18.754 --> 00:15:20.109
that you didn't know before?

00:15:20.109 --> 00:15:23.792
How many of the nine surprising
facts did you not know?

00:15:23.792 --> 00:15:24.625
I'd love to hear from it.

00:15:24.625 --> 00:15:26.057
Share it down in the comments below.

00:15:26.057 --> 00:15:27.247
Also is there something we missed?

00:15:27.247 --> 00:15:29.291
Is there a number 10, number 11

00:15:29.291 --> 00:15:30.516
that you want to add to the list

00:15:30.516 --> 00:15:31.783
that people may not know?

00:15:31.783 --> 00:15:33.290
I'm really curious to find out.

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:34.673
Share that in the comments too.

00:15:34.673 --> 00:15:36.327
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:15:36.327 --> 00:15:37.516
I believe in you.

00:15:37.516 --> 00:15:39.450
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:41.666
and whatever your one word is.

00:15:41.666 --> 00:15:43.941
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:15:43.941 --> 00:15:46.191
(zooming)

